      "html": "<p>A customer who says the A/C is not cold needs gauges, a vent temperature, and a check that the compressor is engaging. A customer who says the heat is weak needs the engine temperature, the coolant level, and the feel of both heater hoses. A customer who says the airflow is weak needs the cabin filter checked first, then the blower, then the evaporator for freeze-up. A customer who says it smells musty needs the drain and the evaporator checked, not the refrigerant.</p>\n<p>In each case the first test is cheap and quick, and it rules out a whole family of faults before any part is touched. The technician who tests first and replaces second is the one who fixes cars once, not twice.</p>\n"
